Fig.~\ref{fig_comparison} compares patch sizes generated by each algorithm. Two variants of the \textit{bpatch} are presented: the standard \textit{"bpatch"}, which employs the basic UNIX diff command, and the enhanced \textit{"bpatch\_m"}, which incorporates the "minimal" option (available using option "-d"). This option applies an optimized variant of the diff algorithm to further compress the set of changes, potentially at the cost of increased processing time. Attempts to use alternative differential algorithms, such as the pure Myers algorithm described in \cite{ref20} (UNIX diff strategies propose a slight variation of Myers algorithm), did not yield significant improvements over \textit{bpatch\_m}, thus, they were excluded from the analysis.

