In terms of model efficiency, inference speed and computational resource consumption are the crucial factors for deploying BRPE modules in real-world applications. This is due to the limited computational resources and computational inference time constraints typically encountered in practical scenarios of blind estimation of RIR. Thus, we compared the inference speed and GPU memory usage of the baselines and the proposed MASS-BRPE module to comprehensively evaluate the deployment performance.

