According to the covariation formula \cite[p. 87]{samoradnitsky1994stable},
the spatial measure remains computationally unchanged up to a scale parameter independent of the direction.
We consequently choose to use $\tilde{\mbx}_{ft} \triangleq \mbx_{ft} / \Vert \mbx_{ft} \Vert_p^p$, where $p < \alpha$ since the norm can be theoretically infinite for $p\geq\alpha$.
