\end{figure}

We also explored the performance of encoder-based transformer models, specifically BERT and RoBERTa, for this classification task. In our experiments, we fine-tuned both BERT and RoBERTa base models on our dataset using a learning rate of $2 \times 10^{-5}$. Both models were trained for 5 epochs, using a stratified split based on the target variable, with a ratio of 0.2 for the validation set. BERT achieved an average F1 score of 0.9048, and RoBERTa achieved an average F1 score of 0.8794.

