For sampling-based approaches, the initial domain for all examples was set to $[-10,10]^n$, but subsequent samples (counterexamples) are drawn from $\mathbb{R}^n$. We selected $3{,}000$ initial samples for LP-CEGIS/LP-CEGIS-SR and $300$ for Z3-CEGIS/Z3-CEGIS-SR, as the latter is considerably slower and significantly impacted by the number of constraints and decision variables. We do a total of 10 CEGIS steps for all iterative synthesis approaches.  While LP\footnote{For the examples in this paper, we solved LP using \texttt{scipy.optimize.linprog} \cite{virtanen2020scipy} with the HiGHS solver \cite{huangfu2023highs}.} 
