Results in Table~\ref{tab:stability} show that incorporating symbolic reduction clearly increases the likelihood of discovering a valid Lyapunov function in most cases. Furthermore, Table~\ref{tab:lasalle} shows that with symbolic reduction, all approaches using LaSalle's principle successfully find a Lyapunov function, whereas approaches without LaSalle fail to do so. Finally, we also conducted extensive tests to evaluate the effect of symbolic reduction on instability detection using Z3. As shown in Table \ref{tab:instability}, symbolic reduction significantly improves performance, enabling successful verification even for high-dimensional systems, while the baseline approach without reduction fails (100\% timeout) even in low dimensions. 


