is less than equal to $n$. Consequently, by Proposition \ref{keres}, 
 the  searches in the red-black tree $RBT3$ take  $O(n \, \mathrm{log} \, n )$   time.

Furthermore, 
\begin{quote}
the number of multiplications  $\leq
 \sum _{\s(a_1, \ldots, a_m) \dot{\rightarrow} a
\in  R\langle E \cup F, \emptyset\rangle} m\leq 
size(R\langle E \cup F, \emptyset \rangle)\leq 
2n$
