\noindent 
Thus, the number of multiplications is less than or equal to $n$.

 For each $a\in C\langle E\cup F, \emptyset\rangle$, the number of comparisons of nonnegative integers during computing the value of the attribute $a.keeps_E$ is equal to 
the number of rules in $R\langle  E \cup F, \emptyset    \rangle$ with right-hand side $a$. 
