\section{Main Case 4}\label{tel}
 In this main case, $E$ and $F$ are  GTESs over  a  signature   $\Sigma$ such that  
  $\S$ has a symbol of arity at least $2$,
  and GTRS  $ R \langle E, F \rangle$ and GTRS $ R \langle F, E \rangle$  are not total.   We assume that we have already run  Algorithm CAD  on $\Sigma$, $E$, and $F$,  and have obtained all the output it produces, see Proposition \ref{kecskemet}.
 Example
\ref{7twoketto} and its  sequel Example   \ref{7twokettofolytatas},  furthermore, Example 
 \ref{8threeharom} and its sequels Examples \ref{8threeharomfolytatas} and  \ref{8threeharommasodikfolytatas}
demonstrate  this case.
\begin{exa}\label{8threeharommasodikfolytatas}\rm 
We continue Examples \ref{8threeharom} and  \ref{8threeharomfolytatas}. We recall that
\begin{quote}
$f(\#, \mathsterling) \tthue {E\cup F} f(\$, \flat)$,\;
$(f(\#, \mathsterling), f(\$, \flat))\not\in  \tthue E  $, \, and \, 
$(f(\#, \mathsterling), f(\$, \flat))\not\in  \tthue F  $.
\end{quote}
The idea of the  $(\Rightarrow)$ direction of the  proof of the next theorem comes from the proof of the above observation.
