\subsection{Agent Reward}
At each time step, each AP agent receives a reward ($r_{t}^{m}$) based on its interaction with the environment. This reward is an average of the total reward for all agents, i,e. $r_{t}^{m} =\dfrac{1}{M} \sum_{m=1}^{M}  r_{t}^{m}$ where,  

\begin{equation}
    r_{t}^{m}= \begin{cases} +\mathrm{z} , & \text{if tx succeeds, (i.e., $R_{m,m} \geq R_{th}$)} \\
    0 & \text{tx fails }\\
0 &  \text{otherwise} \\
    \end{cases}
\end{equation}. 
%To limit the number of times AP agents send CSI updates to the CC for power control assignment, we have added a penalty in equation (5).
The agent is awarded a positive value ($+z$) when there is a successful transmission to encourage agents toward transmission. However, failed transmissions are punished. 

