\section{Conclusion}
\label{sec:06_conclusion}
This paper envisions a knowledge-guided multi-agent framework named \ours{} for automated requirements development. \ours{} 
aims to address gaps in current automation systems for SE, which prioritize code development and overlook the complexities of requirements tasks. \ours{} is composed of six specialized agents and an artifact pool to improve efficiency and accuracy. Specifically, \ours{} outlines the functionality, actions, and knowledge of each agent and provides the conceptual design of the artifact pool. Our case study highlights the potential of KGMAF in real-world scenarios. Finally, we outline several research opportunities for implementing and enhancing automated requirements development using multi-agent systems. We believe that {\sc KGMAF} will play a pivotal role in shaping the future of automated requirements development in the era of LLMs.

