In computation of square matrices, we found that the performance of \OUR designs was ideal, except for the memory bandwidth constraint caused by the large PE layout. We then evaluate the performance for non-square matrices. Fig.~\ref{gemm_a10r} shows the result gained by multiplications of $m \times k$ and $k \times n$ matrices where $m$ and $k$ are fixed at $m=k=4096$ and only $n$ is varied between 32 and 4096. In this evaluation, we set $M_{{\tt Tile}}=128$ in all designs. 

