\subsubsection{Standard Gradient-Descent Training}  
Once the training data and loss function are prepared, we apply standard gradient descent to optimize the model parameters over mini-batches. Gradients are computed via backpropagation, and parameters are updated iteratively until convergence. In practice, we implement this process in PyTorch using the commands \texttt{loss.backward()} and \texttt{optimizer.step()}.



