Our model—based on a DDM - demonstrates strong inpainting performance across a range of gap durations. When comparing to the diffusion-based approach of~\cite{moliner2023diffusion}, we observe comparable or superior performance, particularly in terms of the FAD. While~\cite{moliner2023diffusion} reported a FAD of approximately 4.9 for a 300~ms gap, our method achieves a significantly lower FAD of \textbf{3.81}, indicating more realistic reconstructions. In general, our method AIDD out performs CQT-Diff+ across all metrics. Although our method will benefit from a larger corpus of music, even a small dataset such as \textit{MusicNet}~\cite{dataset} was enough to allow the DDM to learn effectively.


