We now give a new combinatorial characterization of synchronizing morphisms with finite delay on $\morph(\La)$, for any $\La\subseteq \{a,b\}^*$.
This characterization is based on the powers of single letters occurring in $\La$ in the case of non-recognizable primitivity-preserving morphisms, while it is based on the $\morph$-power words in the case of non-primitivity-preserving morphisms.

