\begin{definition}The {\em BWT additive sensitivity function} and {\em BWT multiplicative sensitivity function} for a morphism $\mu$ are,  respectively, the functions $$AS_\mu(n) = \max_{w \in \Sigma^n}(\Delta_{\mu}^+(w))\text{ \ and \ } MS_\mu(n) = \max_{w \in \Sigma^n}(\Delta_{\mu}^\times(w))$$
\end{definition}

Note that the additive sensitivity function is always a non-negative function, as for every $n$, $\Delta_{\mu}^+(a^n)\geq 0$ for any letter $a$.

